4768:
If you guys look hard at the "pink" and "green" overlays, you'll probably find that the colors are actually thin protective plastic coverings the are to be removed pryor to us. Thus there was only one color, White background.

----- Original Message ----
From: Mike White <mike@star-one-edm.com>
To: ballyalley@yahoogroups.com
Sent: Monday, November 19, 2007 4:36:16 PM
Subject: [ballyalley] Re: Astrovision Instructions













            Paul;



There were THREE different overlays for Bally-Astrobasic. The white 

ones are the most common while the pink and the pale green ones are 

much rarer. The rare ones seemed to appear in about 1983 I believe, 

as I was unaware of anything but white before then. Even at 

the "Astro-bash" (SEP 83) I don't remember seeing anything but white. 

I'll look to see if I have a pale green one in Don Gladden's old 

stuff, but I may have sold every one that had one.



Mike W.





